{"id":"jamb-use-of-english","title":"JAMB Use of English: lexis, structure and comprehension","subject":"English","label":"JAMB · WAEC","exams":["jamb","waec"],"language":"en","seconds":180,"duration":180.39,"audio":"voice.mp3","words":458,"sections":[{"id":"hook","title":"The puzzle","start":0,"end":16.395},{"id":"explain","title":"The paper","start":16.395,"end":64.135},{"id":"explain2","title":"Lexis and structure","start":64.135,"end":97.625},{"id":"example","title":"Worked example","start":97.625,"end":117.565},{"id":"check","title":"Quick check","start":117.565,"end":126.785},{"id":"answer","title":"Answer","start":126.785,"end":135.735},{"id":"mistakes","title":"Common mistakes","start":135.735,"end":153.315},{"id":"recap","title":"Recap","start":153.315,"end":180.39}],"lines":[{"s":0,"a":0.5,"b":5.56,"text":"Ada reads a comprehension passage twice, yet still picks the wrong answer. Why?","w":[0.6,0.9,1.2,1.28,1.98,2.42,3.18,3.4,3.68,3.96,4.08,4.42,5.18]},{"s":0,"a":6.01,"b":10.73,"text":"I'm Kora. Today we fix that, and we tighten your lexis and structure too.","w":[6.1,6.28,7.14,7.42,7.58,7.82,8.64,8.76,8.92,9.2,9.36,9.84,9.98,10.42]},{"s":0,"a":11.03,"b":15.97,"text":"This is JAMB Use of English, the paper every UTME candidate must sit.","w":[11.08,11.34,11.52,11.94,12.1,12.26,13.02,13.16,13.72,14.1,14.82,15.36,15.62]},{"s":1,"a":16.82,"b":19.99,"text":"Use of English is compulsory for every UTME candidate.","w":[16.94,17.14,17.3,17.66,17.78,18.42,18.7,19.04,19.56]},{"s":1,"a":20.29,"b":25.7,"text":"The paper has comprehension passages, a cloze passage, and questions on the set reading text.","w":[20.3,20.44,20.8,21.04,21.72,22.58,22.68,23.12,23.78,23.96,24.48,24.58,24.72,24.96,25.28]},{"s":1,"a":26,"b":35.2,"text":"It also tests lexis and structure: synonyms nearest in meaning, antonyms opposite in meaning, sentence interpretation, and filling gaps.","w":[26.08,26.2,26.54,26.96,27.58,27.72,28.92,29.46,29.86,29.96,30.86,31.44,31.92,32.02,32.88,33.32,34.2,34.4,34.74]},{"s":1,"a":35.5,"b":39.85,"text":"Oral forms appear too: vowels, consonants, rhyme, and stress.","w":[35.58,35.88,36.26,36.66,37.42,38.04,38.78,39.16,39.32]},{"s":1,"a":40.15,"b":43.65,"text":"For comprehension, read the questions first, then the passage.","w":[40.16,40.32,41.42,41.64,41.76,42.18,42.84,43,43.12]},{"s":1,"a":43.95,"b":46.88,"text":"Answer from the passage, not from what you already know.","w":[44.04,44.32,44.46,44.58,45.5,45.76,45.92,46.08,46.24,46.6]},{"s":1,"a":47.18,"b":51.1,"text":"When the writer implies something, find the exact line that supports it.","w":[47.22,47.4,47.54,47.94,48.48,49.02,49.3,49.46,50.04,50.34,50.52,50.98]},{"s":1,"a":51.4,"b":55.5,"text":"With a cloze passage, read the whole sentence before choosing the missing word.","w":[51.42,51.62,51.72,52.12,52.98,53.2,53.36,53.6,54.04,54.44,54.82,54.92,55.22]},{"s":1,"a":55.8,"b":59.96,"text":"If two options look true, choose the one the passage actually supports.","w":[55.86,56,56.26,56.64,56.88,57.68,58.02,58.2,58.34,58.46,59.02,59.4]},{"s":1,"a":60.26,"b":63.71,"text":"Your own knowledge can mislead you, so stay inside the text.","w":[60.32,60.62,60.82,61.28,61.48,61.9,62.24,62.48,62.8,63.18,63.3]},{"s":2,"a":64.56,"b":68.19,"text":"In synonym and antonym questions, read the instruction twice.","w":[64.64,64.84,65.4,65.62,66.04,66.9,67.14,67.26,67.74]},{"s":2,"a":68.49,"b":72.99,"text":"Choosing a synonym when the question asks for the opposite is the classic trap.","w":[68.56,68.96,69.08,69.6,69.76,69.86,70.44,70.76,70.9,71.12,71.84,71.96,72.1,72.6]},{"s":2,"a":73.29,"b":76.64,"text":"Use the sentence context to choose between close words.","w":[73.48,73.64,73.8,74.22,74.82,75.02,75.4,75.8,76.16]},{"s":2,"a":76.94,"b":79.79,"text":"For structure, match the verb to the real subject.","w":[76.98,77.16,78,78.32,78.44,78.76,78.9,79.02,79.28]},{"s":2,"a":80.09,"b":84.97,"text":"Say: The box of pens is on the desk. The subject is box, not pens.","w":[80.2,80.6,80.74,81.08,81.22,81.54,81.68,81.78,81.88,82.76,82.92,83.34,83.52,84.3,84.5]},{"s":2,"a":85.27,"b":87.72,"text":"Also say: Each of the boys has a pen.","w":[85.36,85.72,86.42,86.62,86.72,86.84,87.16,87.34,87.4]},{"s":2,"a":88.02,"b":93.22,"text":"Learn correct prepositions: congratulate on, comply with, prefer tea to coffee.","w":[88.06,88.34,88.7,89.76,90.62,91.08,91.54,92.12,92.52,92.7,92.82]},{"s":2,"a":93.52,"b":97.2,"text":"And keep advice, the noun, separate from advise, the verb.","w":[93.54,93.72,93.98,94.64,94.8,95.48,95.84,96.02,96.68,96.82]},{"s":3,"a":98.05,"b":99.88,"text":"Try this structure question with me.","w":[98.14,98.4,98.58,99.04,99.46,99.66]},{"s":3,"a":100.18,"b":102.72,"text":"One of my friends live or lives in Enugu.","w":[100.28,100.42,100.54,100.74,101.12,101.62,101.8,102.24,102.36]},{"s":3,"a":103.02,"b":106.86,"text":"Find the subject first. The subject is one, not friends.","w":[103.1,103.38,103.52,104,104.86,105.02,105.46,105.68,106.08,106.36]},{"s":3,"a":107.16,"b":109.93,"text":"One is singular, so the verb is lives.","w":[107.32,107.54,107.7,108.5,108.68,108.8,109.22,109.4]},{"s":3,"a":110.23,"b":111.99,"text":"One of my friends lives in Enugu.","w":[110.32,110.46,110.56,110.76,111.16,111.46,111.56]},{"s":3,"a":112.29,"b":117.14,"text":"The plural word friends is only inside the phrase, so it does not control the verb.","w":[112.32,112.5,112.88,113.2,113.86,114.08,114.36,114.78,114.9,115.72,115.9,116,116.22,116.4,116.76,116.86]},{"s":4,"a":117.99,"b":120.71,"text":"Now your quick check. Choose the correct verb.","w":[118.04,118.24,118.46,118.72,119.5,119.82,119.94,120.32]},{"s":4,"a":121.01,"b":123.66,"text":"The list of items is or are on the table.","w":[121.04,121.18,121.44,121.66,122.08,122.6,122.88,123.12,123.22,123.32]},{"s":4,"a":123.96,"b":126.36,"text":"Pause here and try it. I'll wait.","w":[124.02,124.34,124.64,124.8,125.08,125.78,125.98]},{"s":5,"a":127.21,"b":129.45,"text":"The correct verb is the singular one: is.","w":[127.22,127.34,127.76,128.12,128.24,128.38,128.92,129.26]},{"s":5,"a":129.75,"b":133.26,"text":"The subject is list, singular, so it takes is.","w":[129.78,129.94,130.44,130.58,131.3,132.14,132.32,132.42,132.96]},{"s":5,"a":133.56,"b":135.31,"text":"The list of items is on the table.","w":[133.58,133.72,133.98,134.2,134.58,134.76,134.86,134.98]},{"s":6,"a":136.16,"b":141.8,"text":"First mistake: rushing the instruction. Read it twice, especially synonym or antonym.","w":[136.24,136.52,137.32,137.68,137.8,138.86,139.08,139.18,140,140.56,141.12,141.36]},{"s":6,"a":142.1,"b":146.9,"text":"Second: picking a word that sounds impressive. Choose the word that fits the sentence.","w":[142.2,143,143.34,143.44,143.72,143.94,144.3,145.16,145.46,145.58,145.84,146.04,146.3,146.42]},{"s":6,"a":147.2,"b":152.89,"text":"Third: spending too long on one passage. Give about forty seconds per question, mark and move on.","w":[147.22,147.84,148.3,148.56,148.88,149.06,149.22,150.2,150.4,150.68,151,151.34,151.5,152.06,152.38,152.5,152.78]},{"s":7,"a":153.74,"b":162.14,"text":"Recap. Use of English is compulsory, and it covers comprehension, cloze, set text, lexis, structure, and oral forms.","w":[153.8,154.72,154.92,155.1,155.46,155.58,156.7,156.82,156.94,157.32,158.36,159.14,159.36,159.98,160.7,161.22,161.42,161.68]},{"s":7,"a":162.44,"b":166.93,"text":"Read questions first, answer from the passage, and check the instruction twice.","w":[162.48,162.72,163.2,164.06,164.32,164.48,164.58,165.36,165.52,165.78,165.92,166.42]},{"s":7,"a":167.23,"b":171.68,"text":"Match verbs to the real subject, and learn prepositions and common confusions.","w":[167.32,167.64,167.98,168.12,168.24,168.5,169.2,169.34,169.62,170.36,170.52,170.92]},{"s":7,"a":171.98,"b":176.29,"text":"Exam tip: about forty seconds per question, then mark and move on.","w":[172.08,172.5,173.06,173.38,173.68,174.04,174.18,175.1,175.34,175.72,175.84,176.14]},{"s":7,"a":176.59,"b":179.79,"text":"Keep practising with Knowzone, and walk into that hall ready.","w":[176.64,176.9,177.4,177.54,178.42,178.6,178.88,179.06,179.26,179.52]}],"scenes":[{"at":0.25,"heading":"Ada's puzzle","items":[{"at":0.4,"kind":"text","text":"Ada reads twice but still picks wrong answers."},{"at":5.91,"kind":"text","text":"Fix: comprehension, lexis, structure."},{"at":10.93,"kind":"text","text":"JAMB Use of English: compulsory UTME paper."}]},{"at":16.57,"heading":"The paper","items":[{"at":16.72,"kind":"text","text":"Use of English is compulsory for all UTME candidates."},{"at":20.19,"kind":"text","text":"Comprehension, cloze, set reading text."},{"at":25.9,"kind":"text","text":"Lexis and structure: synonyms, antonyms, gaps."},{"at":35.4,"kind":"text","text":"Oral forms: vowels, consonants, rhyme, stress."}]},{"at":39.9,"heading":"Comprehension","items":[{"at":40.05,"kind":"text","text":"Read the questions first, then the passage."},{"at":43.85,"kind":"text","text":"Answer from the passage, not outside knowledge."},{"at":47.08,"kind":"text","text":"Find the exact line for an implication."},{"at":51.3,"kind":"text","text":"Cloze: read whole sentence first."},{"at":55.7,"kind":"text","text":"If two seem true, pick the one the passage supports"}]},{"at":64.31,"heading":"Lexis traps","items":[{"at":64.46,"kind":"text","text":"Read synonym/antonym instruction twice."},{"at":68.39,"kind":"text","text":"Trap: synonym when opposite is asked."},{"at":73.19,"kind":"text","text":"Use sentence context between close words."}]},{"at":76.69,"heading":"Structure","items":[{"at":76.84,"kind":"text","text":"Match the verb to the real subject."},{"at":79.99,"kind":"text","text":"Subject = box, not pens."},{"at":85.17,"kind":"text","text":"Each of the boys has a pen."},{"at":87.92,"kind":"text","text":"Prepositions: congratulate on, comply with, prefer to."},{"at":93.42,"kind":"text","text":"advice = noun; advise = verb."}]},{"at":97.8,"heading":"Worked example","items":[{"at":100.08,"kind":"text","text":"One of my friends live / lives in Enugu."},{"at":102.92,"kind":"text","text":"Subject = one, not friends."},{"at":107.06,"kind":"text","text":"One is singular → lives."},{"at":110.13,"kind":"text","text":"One of my friends lives in Enugu."},{"at":112.19,"kind":"text","text":"'friends' is in the phrase; it does not control the verb"}]},{"at":117.56,"heading":"Quick check","items":[{"at":117.56,"kind":"question","text":"The list of items ___ on the table. Choose is or are."}]},{"at":126.96,"heading":"Answer","items":[{"at":127.11,"kind":"text","text":"Answer: is."},{"at":129.65,"kind":"text","text":"Subject = list (singular) → is."},{"at":133.46,"kind":"text","text":"The list of items is on the table."}]},{"at":135.91,"heading":"Common mistakes","items":[{"at":136.06,"kind":"wrong","text":"Rushing the instruction"},{"at":142,"kind":"wrong","text":"Picking an impressive word"},{"at":147.1,"kind":"wrong","text":"Spending too long on one passage"}]},{"at":153.49,"heading":"Recap","items":[{"at":153.64,"kind":"text","text":"Comprehension, cloze, set text, lexis, structure, orals"},{"at":162.34,"kind":"text","text":"Read questions first; answer from passage; check instruction"},{"at":167.13,"kind":"text","text":"Match verbs to real subject; learn prepositions."},{"at":171.88,"kind":"tip","text":"About 40 seconds per question, then mark and move on."},{"at":176.49,"kind":"text","text":"Practise with Knowzone; be ready."}]}],"check":{"at":126.61,"seconds":10,"question":"The list of items ___ on the table. Choose is or are.","answer":"is — the subject is list (singular)."},"fps":30,"mouth":"","level":"","credits":[],"voice":"qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b (cloned voice)"}